<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nymphaeum-1261" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nymphaeum-1261.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-13">13 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nicaea and Genoa conclude the Treaty of Nymphaeum against Venice</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Nicaean emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> concluded a trade and defence pact at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nymphaion">Nymphaeum</a>. Genoa promised naval help against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in return for tax-free trade and access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nymphaeum-1261">Treaty of Nymphaeum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-25">25 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nicaean forces under Alexios Strategopoulos recapture Constantinople</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Alexios Strategopoulos, a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-nicaea">Empire of Nicaea</a>, led Nicaean forces to recapture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a> since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> of 1204. The recapture ended the Latin Empire and restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-callann" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-callann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-callann">Battle of Callann</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Callann was fought in 1261 near Kilgarvan in County Kerry, Ireland, where Fínghin Mac Carthaigh, king of Desmond, defeated the Anglo-Norman FitzGeralds.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pokarwis">Battle of Pokarwis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Pokarwis was fought in January 1261 in Natangia, Prussia, during the Great Prussian Uprising against the Teutonic Order.</p></div></li></ol></section>
